<Base title="About" description="Who Ari Ben-Ami is, in a page.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p class="lede">I'm Ari. I run marketing for a dispensary in Grass Valley, California, and I write code when the thing I want doesn't exist yet.</p>

  <p>Half my life in Israel, half in America. Photoshop CS2 at eleven, taught by a graphic designer in the family. Visual Basic at twelve, at summer camp. A C++ book after one day at my mom's office at GE, talking to the engineers. Nobody paid me for any of it until I was eighteen. Living in two cultures taught me that design only works in the language of the people it's for.</p>

  <p>I spent three years co-founding a product for Shopify stores. We raised money and signed clients, and the second round didn't close. I'd do it again.</p>

  <p>At the dispensary I handle marketing: the budget, the brand, pricing, loyalty, the website, the screens in the store, and the numbers. A good share of that budget goes to local nonprofits, and giving it out is my favorite part of the job.</p>

  <p>Off the clock: chess (around 1500 to 1600, blitz with a drink), the Bucks (followed Giannis from draft night to the trade, fear the deer), mechanical watches (a Speedmaster is next), and markets. I'm a value investor who gets as excited about bond yields as about a stock surging, but new technology is the most fun to invest in. Evaluating something new is where my product designer chops get tested.</p>
</Base>
